                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "af41826d-68d8-4615-939a-f46f57a60e58",
                                                "sense_id": "4a43c7ac-117a-346b-a784-05afd1eae37e",
                                                "text": "To be able to profit from the moment of playfulness we combined the card-game UNO with some additional question cards following the standard rules of the game. We chose this well-known card game as basis, because it is easy to play for children, but also addresses adults."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "50e0f6b0-3a42-4351-b44d-34744e320244",
                                                "sense_id": "4a43c7ac-117a-346b-a784-05afd1eae37e",
                                                "text": "Everybody knows how to play UNO but this time there’s a twist, every time you get a ‘Skip’ or ‘Draw’ card you have to take a shot of this …"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "639fed65-8b28-41cc-8599-0596121c6b55",
                                                "sense_id": "4a43c7ac-117a-346b-a784-05afd1eae37e",
                                                "text": "You will get a reverse card in UNO (YESN’T) and then you will eat chicken legs."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
